    a violation of the AKS constitutes a false or fraudulent claim for purposes of the FCA. Actions under the FCA may be brought by the
    government or as a qui tam action by a private individual in the name of the government, who may also share in any monetary recovery.
    Qui tam actions are filed under seal and impose a mandatory duty on the U.S. Department of Justice to investigate such allegations.
    Manufacturers have faced liability under the FCA for providing inaccurate billing or coding information to customers or promoting
    a product off-label. FCA liability is potentially significant in the healthcare industry because the statute provides for treble
    damages and significant mandatory penalties per false or fraudulent claim or statement for violations, as well as exclusion from
