<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#160;</span></p>

<p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Recoverability
of assets that will continue to be used in the Company&#8217;s operations is measured by comparing the carrying value to the future net
undiscounted cash flows expected to be generated by the asset or asset group. Future undiscounted cash flows include estimates of future
revenues, driven by market growth rates, and estimates of future costs. There were no events during the reporting periods that were deemed
to be a triggering event that would require an impairment assessment, other than the impairment of $<span id="xdx_900_eus-gaap--OtherAssetImpairmentCharges_pn5n6_c20240401__20250331_zfqvadaSCqaj" title="Other asset impairment charges"><ix:nonFraction name="us-gaap:OtherAssetImpairmentCharges" contextRef="From2024-04-012025-03-31" id="Fact000970" format="ixt:numdotdecimal" decimals="-5" scale="6" unitRef="USD">0.5</ix:nonFraction></span> million recorded during the year
ended March 31, 2025 associated with certain R&amp;D assets following Management&#8217;s decision to put its VCAP clinical trial on hold.</span></p>

